==Russenorsk==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|crp-rsn|ru|мужи́къ||man, guy}}.

===Noun===
{{head|crp-rsn|noun}}

# [[people]] (?)
#: {{ux|crp-rsn|daabra '''musik'''|good '''people'''}}

===Usage notes===
The only two known sources translate this word as {{m+|nb|folk||people}}, but the original context may refer to one person (see {{m|crp-rsn|мань}}), like the Russian ancestor word refers to one person only (as well as the Norwegian word may refer to one person in some rare contexts). In addition to it, Russenorsk has no clear distinction between singular and plural.

